  "title": "Sandra A NDE 7305",
  "date": "24 mai 1977",
  "content": "Childbirth on epidural with preceding pyelonephritis. After the birth, I had intense pains in the chest. General panic surrounding me. Then nothing anymore. Then I found myself above the table. An intense light; I heard everything that was said; I witnessed my own resuscitation. I saw my body bouncing with the electric shocks. Doctors were talking between each other, 'Do you think it will get back?' 'I'm afraid this will not happen!' I didn't see my daughter I just had birthed, but I knew that she was there beside me. A last shock was shaking my body and then I don't remember anything else. I woke up connected everywhere, with plenty of people around me. I never dared to talk to anybody about this, except to my husband the day of the first anniversary of my daughter, when my husband told me that I had a severe cardiac arrest. I had many after-effects that subsided with time.",
